  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Down the boards – wall passes from the corner and an extra pass",
  "description": "Full court, goalkeeper in the far goal. Line A stands just outside their own goal crease, line B in the corner behind the same goal and line C at the centre line a little in from the boards. A cone in the corner. A passes to B, rounds the cone and gets the ball back. A plays a first-time pass to the next player in line A (D), who plays it straight back in front of A along the boards.\n\nA then plays a first-time pass to C, carries on at speed along the boards and cuts inside. C passes back into A's path, and A takes the ball into the slot and shoots. Switch lines after each turn: A to C, B to A and C to B. Run it just as much mirrored – or both ways at once with a set of lines on each side. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "The receiver shows with the stick where the pass should go."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "The wall passes are first time – no controlling touch."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Keep the tempo high along the boards and cut inside in time."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Take the ball into the slot and shoot – the shot must hit the target."
    }
  ],
